 More shipped product work: [TQEN](https://tqentech.com), [Crave It](https://craveitsyria.com), and [sanitized production architecture case studies](https://github.com/waelabokalam/production-systems-architecture).
+
+## Optional local OpenTelemetry evaluation
+
+The orchestrator, agent calls and both retrieval functions have opt-in spans. By default tracing is disabled and requires no SDK or endpoint. Enable a per-context, in-memory exporter explicitly:
+
+```python
+from orchestrator.observability import LocalTracing
+from orchestrator.orchestrator import process_alert
+
+telemetry = LocalTracing(enabled=True)
+with telemetry.activate():
+    result = process_alert(synthetic_alert)
+spans = telemetry.exporter.get_finished_spans()
+telemetry.shutdown()
+```
+
+Install `requirements-observability.txt` and run `python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider eval/test_observability.py` for the provider-free instrumentation checks. They exercise real orchestration and retrieval functions with deterministic external-provider adapters. Span names are closed constants; only outcomes and document counts are recorded. Prompts, patient IDs, retrieved text, result bodies, exception messages and stack traces are not exported. Existing application session logs are unchanged and must be handled separately. This is an academic prototype with local verification, not a clinical deployment or measured latency improvement.
